The four license files were read from fresh external checkouts at the exact
revisions above. Their complete MIT texts are reproduced below; the digests
and links let an auditor verify the retained text against the pinned sources.

The following paths are the relevant upstream files and types consulted for
the corresponding production modules.

| `rosu-map-api/src` | `src/section/hit_objects/slider/{curve.rs,path.rs}` and `src/util/pos.rs` | `osu.Framework/Utils/{PathApproximator,CircularArcProperties,Precision}.cs`; `osuTK.Vector2.Length` |
| `rosu-pp-api/src/catch/object/juice_stream.rs` | `src/catch/object/juice_stream.rs`; `src/model/hit_object.rs` legacy curve wrapper | `osu.Game.Rulesets.Catch/Objects/JuiceStream.cs`; `osu.Game.Rulesets.Catch/Objects/SliderEventGenerator.cs` |
| `src/lib.rs`, `src/model.rs` | `src/lib.rs`; `src/any/{attributes.rs,score_state.rs}` | `osu.Game/Rulesets/Ruleset.cs`; `osu.Game/Scoring/ScoreInfo.cs` |
| `src/data.rs`, `src/difficulty.rs` | `src/any/{attributes.rs,strains.rs}` and mode-specific `attributes.rs`, `strains.rs` | mode-specific difficulty attributes and calculators |
| `src/performance.rs` | `src/any/performance/mod.rs`; mode-specific performance attributes | mode-specific performance calculators |
| `src/gradual.rs` | `src/any/difficulty/gradual.rs`; `Difficulty::passed_objects` | ruleset difficulty hit-object prefix semantics |
| `src/scoring.rs` | `src/any/score_state.rs`; mode score-state types | mode-specific score processors and hit-result weights |
| `src/hit_windows.rs` | public beatmap attribute builder | `OsuHitWindows.cs`, `TaikoHitWindows.cs`, `ManiaHitWindows.cs`, catch catcher sizing |
| `src/score_multiplier.rs` | structured mod settings supplied through `rosu-mods` | `OsuScoreMultiplierCalculatorV2.cs`, `TaikoScoreMultiplierCalculator.cs`, `CatchScoreMultiplierCalculator.cs`, `ManiaScoreMultiplierCalculator.cs` |

Historical parity evidence (not a production source)
------------------------------------------------------

`tools/oracle/reference/lazer-calculator` is retained as historical parity
evidence only. It records former tosuapp/lazer-calculator behavior for
comparison and audit history; it is **not** the current calculator fixture's
oracle, a production build input, crate dependency, or runtime dependency.
The current generated oracle fixture targets `osu-pp-calculator` 0.6.1 as
pinned in `tools/oracle/oracle-lock.json`. The production workspace does not
include or compile the historical directory. This build boundary does not
by itself prove source independence from the former wrapper.

Project-authored code in the `vosu-pp` package is dual-licensed under
`MIT OR Apache-2.0`; the authoritative texts are at the root `LICENSE-MIT`
and `LICENSE-APACHE`, with matching crate-local copies. These terms do not
change the MIT terms of the upstream inputs above, or relicense any retained
LGPL-derived material. Shared data structures and formula fragments identified
by the provenance audit require source-level review before the former wrapper
can be ruled out as their source.

